{
  "appliance_id": "a8b0c3e2-5b6a-4c9f-8d1e-2f3a4b5c6d7e",
  "name": "IEC 61850 IED Subscriber",
  "category": "guest",
  "description": "IEC 61850 GOOSE/SV traffic subscriber (simulated IED). Listens for the configured APPID on its Ethernet port and reports unique frames, duplicates and round-trip latency to the console. The PRP transparency proof: exactly-once delivery across the redundant network, zero duplicates.",
  "vendor_name": "Arctic3D AB",
  "vendor_url": "https://arctic3d.xyz",
  "product_name": "IEC 61850 IED Subscriber",
  "registry_version": 6,
  "status": "experimental",
  "maintainer": "Arctic3D AB",
  "maintainer_email": "ceo@arctic3d.xyz",
  "usage": "# IEC 61850 IED Subscriber\n\nSimulated IED that listens for real IEC 61850 GOOSE (0x88B8) / SV\n(0x88BA) traffic and reports **unique frames, duplicates and round-trip\nlatency** on the console. Zero duplicates across a PRP network or HSR\nring proves exactly-once delivery. Attach the node to a RedBox SAN port.\nThe telnet aux console (port 5000) gives a shell.\n\n## Environment variables\n\nSet these per node (right-click → Configure → General → Environment):\n\n| Variable | Default | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `IEC_MODE` | `subscriber` | IED personality (publisher or subscriber) |\n| `IEC_APPID` | `0x1001` | APPID to listen for (hex); must match the publisher |\n| `IEC_ET` | `goose` | `goose` (0x88B8) or `sv` (0x88BA) |\n| `IEC_SVID` | `MU01` | SV svID to listen for (SV mode) |\n\n## Verification\n\n- Subscriber console: `total=… unique=… dupes=…` plus latency\n  percentiles (min/p50/p95/max).\n- `dupes=0` across failover tests = PRP/HSR transparency proof.\n- In Wireshark, capture on the SAN: the publisher's frames decode as\n  full GOOSE/SV protocol trees.\n",
  "docker": {
    "adapters": 1,
    "image": "ghcr.io/grymme/prp-sim:latest",
    "console_type": "telnet",
    "environment": "IEC_MODE=subscriber\nIEC_APPID=0x1001\nIEC_ET=goose"
  },
  "symbols": {
    "default": "symbols/iec61850-subscriber.svg"
  }
}
